TITLE:: MapperTarget
summary:: something a controller can move, named by an address
categories:: Libraries>Mapper
related:: Classes/Mapper, Classes/MapperMap, Classes/MapperUnits

DESCRIPTION::
An address, code::[provider, ... path]::, and the mapper it belongs to. The target asks its
provider what the path is now, so it follows what it names when that is rebuilt; when the
provider is gone or has no such path it does not exist, and setting it does nothing.

code::
t = MapperTarget(Mapper.default, [\tidal, \cut]);
t.exists;
t.value = 0.4;
t.label;
::

subsection:: Descriptions

What a provider answers for a path - an Event:

table::
## code::label:: || what it is called
## code::kind:: || code::\knob:: (the default), code::\toggle::, code::\trigger:: or code::\menu::
## code::spec:: || the range a mapping's lo and hi live in, and its warp
## code::get::, code::set:: || Functions, in the target's own units
## code::trigger:: || what a trigger does; without it, set(1)
## code::range:: || where a new mapping's lo and hi start, if not the whole spec
## code::group:: || where it sits in the window's list
## code::owner:: || something else that moves it: then it cannot be mapped
## code::path:: || its path, in what code::mapTargets:: answers
::

